---
title: "Emergency Medical Technician"
code: "EMS-111"
category: "emergency-medical-services"
credits: "7"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/EMS-100"
corequisites:
  - "2026/EMS-120"
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisite: EMS 100/equivalent"
corequisiteNote: "Corequisite: EMS 120"
---

Prepares student for certification as a Virginia and National Registry EMT. Focuses on all aspects of pre-hospital basic life support as defined by the Virginia Office of Emergency Medical Services curriculum for Emergency Medicine Technician. 5 lecture hours; 4 lab hours; 9 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
